# Paths that hold the owner's data, never the application.
#
# In the public code repository these paths are gitignored and, when a private data repository is
# configured (NICHE_MINER_DATA), symlinked from it by `python3 scripts/workspace.py link`.
# `python3 scripts/workspace.py export` leaves them out of the public snapshot, and
# `python3 scripts/workspace.py check` refuses a commit that carries them into a public repository.
#
# One path per line, relative to the repository root. A trailing slash marks a directory: link
# creates it in the data repository when it is missing, so new runs land there from the start.
# A line without the slash is a file: link skips it until the data repository has it.
# Shell-style wildcards (*, ?, [0-9]) match files, as in .gitignore.

config/founder-profile.yaml
runs/
backlog/
reports/
tasks/standing-objective.md
tasks/*-20[0-9][0-9]-*
docs/journal.md
docs/demand-dashboard.html
docs/pipeline-map.html
docs/snapshots/
.privacy-denylist
